I leave the doctor's practice and walk to the pharmacy.
My head still hurts, and I want to go home quickly.
I go inside and give the pharmacist my green prescription.
I have to pay for the medicine myself, because it is a green prescription.
The pharmacist reads the prescription and fetches a small box.
"You should take two tablets a day," he says.
"One in the morning and one in the evening."
"And you should drink a lot."
I just nod, because my throat hurts.
"That makes eight Euro, please," the pharmacist says.
I reach into my dark green coat and take out my wallet.
I pay the eight Euro in cash.
He gives me the medicine and the receipt.
I say thank you and put the box into my coat pocket.
Then I leave the pharmacy.
I walk the last few streets home.
I just want to get into my bed now.
